    "model": {
      "requirement": "One open-weight video model generates the edited pixels directly. Inference scripts are permitted. One attempt, fixed settings/seed across duration-limited segments; log every segment and technical retry.",
      "examples": "Use an open-weight video model your hardware supports, for example MiniMax-H3 (MiniMax, 2026, https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3), JoyAI-Video-Edit (JD Open Source, 2026, https://github.com/jd-opensource/JoyAI-Video-Edit), LTX-2.3 (Lightricks, 2026, in/outpainting IC-LoRA) or Wan2.1-VACE-14B (Wan, arXiv:2503.20314; VACE, Jiang et al., arXiv:2503.07598); other open-weight models are equally welcome. Wan2.1-VACE-1.3B (Apache 2.0) is a smaller option; memory depends on settings (staff trial: 14 GB, 13 min for a 5.5 s cut at 480p, mask + reference image). The staff example with MiniMax-H3 is in data/genai_oracle/.",
